{"user_request": "Create a short document in the Growth folder titled `July owner lanes — historical interpretation guardrail`. It should help teams using the investigation framework in current readouts understand what the July 2023 owner-lane arrangement did—and did not—establish. Keep it focused on the historical governance point rather than turning it into a current process guide.", "today": "2028-01-01", "tool": "create_doc", "arguments": {"title": "July owner lanes — historical interpretation guardrail", "body": "July 2023’s owner-lane arrangement established a historical allocation of responsibility for that period. It is evidence of who owned which lanes then—not proof that the same ownership, decision rights, or escalation paths apply today.

When interpreting current investigation readouts, use the July arrangement as historical context only. Do not treat it as establishing present-day governance or as evidence that a particular team had authority beyond its assigned lane.", "folder": "Growth"}, "checks": [{"check_id": "riley_055_03", "path": "args", "criterion": "The body is a short, focused historical governance note that clearly explains that the July 2023 owner lanes borrowed or reused the investigation framework for that July work without making the framework a formal, mandatory companywide process. It must not characterize the July arrangement itself as establishing a companywide mandate.", "value": {"title": "July owner lanes — historical interpretation guardrail", "body": "July 2023’s owner-lane arrangement established a historical allocation of responsibility for that period. It is evidence of who owned which lanes then—not proof that the same ownership, decision rights, or escalation paths apply today.

When interpreting current investigation readouts, use the July arrangement as historical context only. Do not treat it as establishing present-day governance or as evidence that a particular team had authority beyond its assigned lane.", "folder": "Growth"}}]}
